Relevant columns and their potential usage (only fields mentioned in the task)

ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRACES  
• "from_address": sender of every internal / external call — derive outgoing activity, failures, contract creation, rewards  
• "to_address": receiver — derive incoming activity, counterpart addresses  
• "value": Wei transferred — derive ETH amounts (÷ 1e18)  
• "trace_type": identify “call”, “create”, “reward”, “suicide”, etc.  
• "call_type": filter‑out “delegatecall” | “callcode” | “staticcall” when present  
• "status": success (1) / failure (0) — exclude failures from most metrics, count them separately  
• "gas_used": gas actually consumed — needed for avg / std gas figures  
• "block_timestamp": micro‑seconds since Unix epoch — filter < 1483228800000000 (Jan‑01‑2017) & derive hour‑of‑day  
• "block_number" / "block_hash": optional joins / further checks  

ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TRANSACTIONS  
• "hash": primary key to join with TRACES when gas price or fees are required  
• "from_address", "to_address": same usage as above (externally‑visible layer)  
• "gas_price", "receipt_gas_used": compute paid fee (= gas_price × receipt_gas_used)  
• "receipt_status": keep only 1 (success)  
• "block_timestamp": identical filter < 1483228800000000  

ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.TOKEN_TRANSFERS  
• "from_address", "to_address": outgoing / incoming token flows  
• "token_address": to count distinct ERC‑20 contract addresses  
• "value": token amount (string)  
• "block_timestamp": date filter < 1483228800000000  

ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN.CONTRACTS  
• "address": contract address created  
• "bytecode": length → bytecode_size  
• "block_timestamp": filter < 1483228800000000  
• "block_number", "block_hash": possible joins  

Conditions commonly used  
1. "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000            -- before 2017‑01‑01 UTC  
2. COALESCE("call_type", '') NOT ILIKE ANY ('delegatecall','callcode','staticcall')  
3. "status" = 1                                    -- successful traces  
4. "receipt_status" = 1                            -- successful transactions  

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Example Snowflake SQL snippets (10 separate queries, each limited to 20 rows)

```sql
--Description: 1. Distinct addresses that were active (either sender or receiver) before 2017‑01‑01.
SELECT DISTINCT "from_address" AS "address"
FROM "ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."TRACES"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
UNION
SELECT DISTINCT "to_address" AS "address"
FROM "ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."TRACES"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2. Sample of successful incoming “call” traces with non‑zero value (ETH transfers).
SELECT "to_address",
       "from_address",
       "value",
       "gas_used",
       "block_timestamp"
FROM "ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."TRACES"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "trace_type" = 'call'
  AND "status" = 1
  AND "value" <> 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3. Example of excluding delegatecall/callcode/staticcall.
SELECT "transaction_hash",
       "from_address",
       "to_address",
       "call_type",
       "value"
FROM "ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."TRACES"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "trace_type" = 'call'
  AND COALESCE("call_type", '') NOT ILIKE ANY ('delegatecall','callcode','staticcall')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4. Retrieve hourly breakdown (0–23) for a random address.
SELECT "from_address",
       FLOOR(("block_timestamp" / 1000000) / 3600) % 24 AS "hour_of_day",
       COUNT(*) AS "txn_cnt"
FROM "ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."TRACES"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "from_address" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "from_address", FLOOR(("block_timestamp" / 1000000) / 3600) % 24
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5. Check mining reward traces (trace_type = 'reward') before 2017.
SELECT "to_address" AS "miner",
       SUM("value") / 1e18 AS "total_reward_eth"
FROM "ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."TRACES"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "trace_type" = 'reward'
GROUP BY "to_address"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6. Contracts created by each creator address (trace_type = 'create').
SELECT "from_address" AS "creator",
       COUNT(*) AS "create_count"
FROM "ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."TRACES"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "trace_type" = 'create'
GROUP BY "from_address"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7. Failed transactions initiated by an address (status = 0).
SELECT "from_address",
       COUNT(*) AS "failure_count"
FROM "ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."TRACES"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "status" = 0
GROUP BY "from_address"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8. Bytecode size for contracts created before 2017.
SELECT "address"          AS "contract_addr",
       LENGTH("bytecode") AS "bytecode_size"
FROM "ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."CONTRACTS"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9. Token transfers IN to each address (before 2017) with distinct token types.
SELECT "to_address",
       COUNT(*)                       AS "token_in_tnx",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "token_address") AS "token_in_type"
FROM "ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."TOKEN_TRANSFERS"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
GROUP BY "to_address"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10. Join TRANSACTIONS to compute exact fee (gas_price × receipt_gas_used) for early years.
SELECT "from_address",
       SUM("gas_price" * "receipt_gas_used") / 1e18 AS "total_fee_eth"
FROM "ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."ETHEREUM_BLOCKCHAIN"."TRANSACTIONS"
WHERE "block_timestamp" < 1483228800000000
  AND "receipt_status" = 1
GROUP BY "from_address"
LIMIT 20;
```

